@namespace BlazorCN
@inherits ComponentBaseCn

@* Reference: select.tsx SelectScrollUpButton — "cn-select-scroll-up-button top-0 w-full" with a
   ChevronUp icon. Divergences from Base UI, documented:
   - `sticky` added: the reference arrow is positioned by Base UI outside the scroller; ours lives
     inside the scrolling popup, so sticky pins it to the visible top edge while the list scrolls.
   - Visibility: Base UI unmounts the arrow when the list can't scroll up. We approximate with a
     CSS scroll-state container query (`hidden` by default, shown when the popup — a
     `container-type: scroll-state` container, see SelectContentCn — is scrollable toward `top`).
     Browsers without scroll-state support simply never show the arrow (today's behavior).
   - `pointer-events-none`: Base UI arrows scroll-on-hover via JS; ours is a passive affordance,
     so it must not swallow clicks/hovers on items at the popup edge. *@
<div class="@Cn.Merge("cn-select-scroll-up-button pointer-events-none sticky top-0 w-full hidden [@container_scroll-state(scrollable:top)]:flex", Class)"
     style="@Style"
     data-slot="select-scroll-up-button"
     aria-hidden="true"
     @attributes="AdditionalAttributes">
    <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m18 15-6-6-6 6"/></svg>
</div>
